<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 38 — Service-to-Service Security.
    spiffe/   SPIFFE IDs, the X509-SVID rules, a trust manager that validates SVIDs per trust domain, a key manager
              that rotates SVIDs under a running SSLContext, TLS 1.3 mutual-TLS sockets
    authz/    PeerPolicy: which workload may call which route, deny by default
    token/    certificate-bound access tokens (RFC 8705) and a single-flight client-credentials token cache
    pki/      DevCa: a JDK-only development CA that issues SPIFFE SVIDs for tests and measurements (not production)
    web/      payment-service (mutual TLS via Spring Boot SSL bundles, peer policy filter, resource server) and
              order-service's client (SSL bundle + client-credentials interceptor, rebuilt on SVID rotation)
  resources/spire and resources/istio hold the SPIRE and Istio configuration. verify/run.sh measures everything
  except web/ with a JDK alone.
-->
